{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1383890-goetic-gods-legacy","id":1383890,"title":"Goetic Gods Legacy.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-25T18:46:28-07:00","id":1383890,"title":"Goetic Gods Legacy.","content":"So,we have a legacy that takes the Goetia of their own negative feelings and gives them physical shape. I have another take on the idea.a legacy looking for the goetia of god,but with a twist. Those guys,they believe very few people truly think about gods all that much. Even those who claim to be religious think mostly about their own issues. But some people well and truly center the lives around one divinity or more,thinking about those gods damn near 24/7. That legacy then find the Oneiros of those true religious people. They study the individual goetia of each Oneiros. Then they go to the Temenos to find the God goetia of the shared human mind. <br /> Let's take thor as example,even at the height of his worship,not many people truly thought about Thor a lot. So,the Temeno's Thor is just an strong dude with a hammer that can control lightening. But the individual Thor of a true believer is truly awe inspiring,a mix of giant and man that bleeds lightening. They want the &quot;main&quot; Thor to be like this. They want the shared ideal of Thor to be like he is in the mind of a true believer<br /> But,what attainments would they have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-25-2020, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T21:17:08-07:00","id":1383904,"title":"","content":"You could make them physical via Mind and Life. You could use Mind and Spirit to make them constantly manifest in a durable form.<br /> <br /> I would probably favor Mind and Life, then use a Weaving to let people bodily enter their Astral Realms if they are in a locale suitably connected to them. So if you go to an exhibit of Norse mythology, you could end up joining Thor in his trials with Uthgard-Loki or enjoy endless feasting in Valhalla, etc. <br /> <br /> But more than anything, I think the first step is pinning down a methodology. How do they study these gods ? What do they want to do with said knowledge? Make Thor be born into the world to spread his new image ? Make followers gain Thor powers to do this for him ? Transform themselves into avatar of these gods ? If so, how do they differ from the Bene Elohim or Caretakers ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T21:21:15-07:00","id":1383905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1383890-goetic-gods-legacy?p=1383904#post1383904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could make them physical via Mind and Life. You could use Mind and Spirit to make them constantly manifest in a durable form.<br /> <br /> I would probably favor Mind and Life, then use a Weaving to let people bodily enter their Astral Realms if they are in a locale suitably connected to them. So if you go to an exhibit of Norse mythology, you could end up joining Thor in his trials with Uthgard-Loki or enjoy endless feasting in Valhalla, etc. <br /> <br /> But more than anything, I think the first step is pinning down a methodology. How do they study these gods ? What do they want to do with said knowledge? Make Thor be born into the world to spread his new image ? Make followers gain Thor powers to do this for him ? Transform themselves into avatar of these gods ? If so, how do they differ from the Bene Elohim or Caretakers ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been developing their goals. You see they believe Gods and morality are quintessentially tied. They think for people to fighy back against oppression,they NEED a Thor or a Hercules. To people for be compassionate they NEED a Durga or an Hestia. They don't want to be gods,they want gods to exist to inspire people to be their best selves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T22:35:17-07:00","id":1383911,"title":"","content":"Interesting, they want to find the right gods, get them to manifest and inspire humanity to self improvement.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, here are my first ideas for Attainments:<br /> <br /> Mind 1: A variation of Know Nature, but instead it answers questions about the vision of a god the target hold in their mind. <br /> <br /> Life 1: After a ceremony, this allows target to speak to any creatures that serve their god, gaining [Life] extra dice on Animal Ken rolls. This is a variation of Speak with Beasts with a restriction to make up for the extra Reach.<br /> <br /> Mind 2: Allows the mage and the target to enter either of their Oneiroi after a ceremony to the god. This is a variation of Astral Adept.<br /> <br /> Life 2: Spend a scene to connect a target with a god they hold in their mind. This grants them a variation of the Daimon merit, but can only be used up to the entity's Rank times per session. This is a Ruling of Mind with advanced duration.<br /> <br /> Mind 3: After a ceremony, the target gains [Mind] Numina and/or Influence dots that their god vision has. A Weaving of Mind and Life with Reach assigned to advanced duration.<br /> <br /> Life 3: Allows bodily travel to the Astral domain of a god in any area that is Resonant with them. A Weaving of Life and Mind with Reach assigned to instant use.<br /> <br /> Mind 4: After spending time in a ceremony to a god and a mana, you can grant a skill that god has. This can allow the target to go over their limit. This is a variation of Gain Skill with a restriction to make up for the extra Reach.<br /> <br /> Life 4: Allow goetia to exist as living beings, maintaining all the advantages of an ephemeral body. A Patterning of Life and Mind, with some elements of Shapechanging to represent avatars.<br /> <br /> Mind 5: Social Networking with advanced duration, so the gods always have access to the right allies to carry out their visions.<br /> <br /> Life 5: With a ceremony and a mana, it allows the Astral domain of a god to manifest in organic incarnations. Like a living Lair. A Patterning of Life &amp; Mind with Reach assigned to indefinite duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-26-2020, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T03:30:48-07:00","id":1383931,"title":"","content":"I'd not move Astral gods out of the Astral. They are at their most powerful there. Instead I'd focus on finding true believers with the first few attainments, and then the latter part of the legacy would be focused on Temenotic terraforming to be performed on the gods to fit more closely with the visions of their gods of the true believers, which if done right also more closely connects those gods to a greater &quot;audience.&quot; So for instance you might round up a bunch of info on Hermes from individual believers in Hermes, and then go to the Temenos realm of Hermes and give him a bullet point plan for expanding his holdings in the Temenos realm of travel or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T09:00:43-07:00","id":1383962,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dreamspeaker_(MTAw)\" target=\"_blank\">Dreamspeakers</a> might be along the lines of what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T10:43:11-07:00","id":1383975,"title":"","content":"Yep, it all depends on the angle they want to focus on. <br /> <br /> My original idea was to grow and change their legend by bringing it to the physical world as miracles.<br /> <br /> If they want to focus on redefining the astral image to then affect the collective unconscious, then Mrmdubois has a pretty solid way of doing it.<br /> <br /> But if they are focused on being emissaries for these being, then as proindrakenzol mentioned, the Dreamspeakers are specialists in that.<br /> <br /> They are all very viable roads to help push a more inspiring image of Astral gods.<br /> <br /> <i>Observation:</i> I noticed I had forgotten to add a Mind 4 Attainment idea and edited one in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-26-2020, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}